WEBVTT

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.780
And so, and so...

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.400
Kentarou-kun just wouldn’t let go of me!

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.780
Jinko, you were the one who wouldn’t let go of Kentarou-kun.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:17.820
You’re one to talk, considering you wasted no time giving your cell phone number to Taketo-kun.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.580
It’s not like that. He asked me for my number.

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:28.360
I never knew the ski circle would be this much fun.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.670
There are so many cool guys there.

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.600
How’s it going on your side, Kotoko?

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.510
I guess that face speaks for itself...

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:19.780
I’m so glad I didn’t go with Kotoko to join the tennis club.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:22.200
Hey, you two!

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.930
All I’ve been hearing is that you’re joining these circles just to get boys.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.710
Your motives are impure!

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:36.670
Since you say that, then who’s the one who joined the tennis club just to go after Irie?

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:40.640
You’re the most impure one.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.290
That’s...

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:47.280
I would never consider joining a hard club after getting into college.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:50.840
I didn’t think it’d be this hard.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.210
Aihara-san.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.070
Sudou-sempai!

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:58.300
Why are you jumping to attention like that?

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.030
Ah, no, it’s...

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:03.740
Your face looks terrible. Are you all right?

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:07.080
I guess our training is a bit hard.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.550
But, don’t get discouraged and keep coming, okay?

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:10.280
Yes.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:12.930
Okay. See you later then.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:14.440
He seems like a nice guy.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.540
Not at all!

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.830
It seems like he must have forgotten, but...

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:21.340
...he’s the one who did this to my face!

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:25.680
You don’t say! But, he looks so kind.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.180
It’s true though!

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:31.540
I’ll be testing your abilities today.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.640
Freshmen, please enter the court.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:34.520
Yes!

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:41.330
Okay, newcomers. Here I go.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:55.730
Sudou-sempai’s personality changes whenever he holds a racquet.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:01.310
Do you girls even have eyes on your heads?!

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.840
You there! Fight!

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:09.450
Amazing.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:10.180
Aihara!

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:17.770
Don’t daydream!

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.010
It’s not a laughing matter!

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:28.660
Because of this face...

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:39.630
Umm, this is...

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.780
No!

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:03.570
Both my heart and body are in shambles.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:06.840
If it’s really that tough, then why don’t you just quit?

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:11.540
Then again, it’s not that easy to quit because Irie is there?

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:17.910
Irie-kun looks so cool when he’s playing tennis.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:20.380
Are you laughing or crying? Choose one.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.430
Not here, huh?

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.940
If you’re looking for the second volume, I have it.

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:35.240
You can borrow it if you’d like.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.310
You’ll need it to write the report, won’t you?

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:39.080
Thanks.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:49.780
Hey, how come you’re practicing on court?

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:54.880
I’m practicing for the beginner’s tournament from today onwards.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:57.120
Beginner’s tournament?

00:05:57.510 --> 00:06:00.120
It’s got nothing to do with you though.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:04.640
I wonder if you’ll even set foot on court before you graduate.

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:06.380
Will Irie-kun be participating too?

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:10.970
Come to think of it, where’s Irie-kun?

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.190
Oh, you didn’t hear?

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:18.270
He joined under the condition that he’ll only attend whenever he feels like it and for competitions.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:19.560
In other words, a special case.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.610
Really?

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:26.490
You know nothing about him despite living together.

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:31.810
That would mean, your relationship is only that deep?

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:37.750
What the heck? Only when Irie-kun feels like it?

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:40.510
Wouldn’t it have been more accurate to say that he’ll never attend?

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:53.180
Aihara! Why are you slacking off?!

00:06:55.810 --> 00:07:00.480
Joining the tennis club is pointless if Irie-kun isn’t going to come.

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:03.680
I’m such a fool.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:06.860
Hey, you wanna go watch that movie?

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.360
Ah, Metal Heart?

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:11.820
I heard that it was interesting.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:15.570
It’s a love story recommended for couples.

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:22.290
Movie?

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.790
It’s showing until Sunday.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.860
Would you like to go together?

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:27.870
Not interested.

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:30.550
But, it’s really popular!

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:34.500
It’s a love story about a handsome cyborg and a college student.

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:37.060
And, the actor looks just you!

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:40.810
He even has a cold personality like you.

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:44.310
Are you trying to sneak in an insult?

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.250
Of course not.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:48.580
If you want to go watch, then why don’t you just go by yourself?

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:52.330
Come on. You didn’t have to be so blunt.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:53.280
You’re bothering me.

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:03.080
He really is cold.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:11.630
Thanks.

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:14.300
You’re welcome.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.350
So, you’ll go out with me this Sunday, right?

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:22.310
I lent you my book and
I get no thanks in return?

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.310
I just said my thanks earlier.

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:29.240
The thanks I want are a little greater than that.

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:35.090
I received a pair of movie tickets, but didn’t have anyone to go with.

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:37.700
I thought of just giving them to my sister.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:40.490
But, I’m glad I didn’t.

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:43.690
Irie-kun, you’ll go with me, right?

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:48.860
Huh? Wait. I can’t really hear you.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:55.930
Eh? But you said that you would be free on Sunday.

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:58.690
Really? Okay then.

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:00.430
Take care.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:10.120
I should have just slept in if Jinko and Satomi weren’t going to come.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:15.100
I wanted to go on a date with Irie-kun too.

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:21.230
I’d have a fashion show for Irie-kun on the night before.

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:26.330
Wear a little make-up, and walk cheerily alongside him.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.710
Yes, just like that!

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:36.680
Why?

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.710
Why are Irie-kun and Matsumoto Yuuko...?

00:09:39.710 --> 00:09:40.770
Why?

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:43.230
Sudou-sempai.

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:45.470
Oh, Aihara.

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:48.850
Why? Why is Irie the only one popular with the girls?

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:51.900
Actually, why are you here?

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:54.400
It’s because I’m following Matsumoto.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:59.100
Sempai, don’t tell me you’re stalking Matsumoto-san?

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:00.210
No!

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:05.500
While I was searching for the right moment to ask her out on a date...

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.060
...I ended up here.

00:10:11.030 --> 00:10:13.880
The reason why he asked me to go by myself...

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:18.260
...was because he already had a date with Matsumoto Yuuko?

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:21.270
Aihara, this isn’t any time
to be standing around.

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:22.780
We’re going too!

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:26.770
How can we leave them alone together in the darkness of the cinema?

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:30.240
But, the line for the ticket counter is so long.

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:31.520
We’ll never make it.

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:35.690
Sempai, those tickets!

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:37.190
Don’t ask!

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:38.060
But...

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:40.390
Is this any time to be confused?

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:43.450
I’ll go by myself if you’re not going!

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:47.160
Let’s go, Sempai!

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:10.100
Oh, sorry. I dropped my pamphlet.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:11.840
Nice, Aihara!

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:12.980
Thank you.

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:35.010
That movie was unexpectedly shallow.

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:36.120
Really?

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:39.270
If they had made it with more scientific basis...

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:41.700
...I think the story would have had more depth.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:47.600
In the end, it was mainly about love being able to overcome all obstacles...

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:55.310
I’ll never wash my left hand ever again!

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:56.650
Wash it, please!

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:00.540
I thought it was pretty interesting.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:03.650
I’d like to build a cyborg like that too.

00:12:03.650 --> 00:12:05.930
It’s scary since you might just be able to do it.

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:08.910
Sempai, let’s go!

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.800
Say, what do you want to be in the future?

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:15.630
I don’t know.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:17.270
You don’t know?

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:21.440
Don’t you want to be a politician, or a university lecturer, for instance?

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:22.380
Not really.

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.500
You could be a lawyer or even a physician.

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:27.930
There’s nothing that you can’t become, right?

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:29.220
I wonder about that.

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:32.960
Hey, Irie-kun...

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:36.980
What kind of girl would be your type?

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:40.580
Let me see...

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:45.120
I’d prefer a girl who’s pretty, glamorous and intelligent.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:48.370
Oh, and good at cooking too.

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:52.120
I prefer intelligent guys by far.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:54.410
Not those old man types though.

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:57.100
Definitely a no for guys with mustaches.

00:12:57.970 --> 00:13:02.270
Could we be the ideal couple?

00:13:02.270 --> 00:13:03.480
Perhaps.

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:06.750
But...

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:07.940
But?

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:09.500
Nevermind.

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:11.190
What do you want to do after this?

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:14.120
I’d like to buy a new racquet.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:15.720
Would you accompany me?

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:16.860
Sure.

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:19.050
Let’s get going then.

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:27.620
What’s with this lovey-dovey atmosphere?

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:35.330
Careful!

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:40.310
Thanks.

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:43.700
What’s with that hand?!

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:46.670
What am I doing?

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:50.290
I’m spying on other people’s dates.

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:53.350
And in the end, I’m shown how close they are.

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:56.910
Aihara!

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:58.340
What’s wrong?

00:13:58.340 --> 00:13:59.980
I’m going home.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:02.730
How can you be saying that now?!

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:05.700
I can’t stand watching this any more.

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:10.170
There’s nothing we can do if they like each other.

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:14.050
Then, you’re recognizing their relationship?!

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:16.860
But...

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:21.790
I don’t want to feel any more miserable than this.

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:23.260
Aihara.

00:14:23.260 --> 00:14:24.360
I’m leaving!

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:26.600
Sorry.

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:32.630
I’m sorry!

00:14:33.460 --> 00:14:36.110
Sorry for getting your shirt wet.

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:38.810
So, what ya gonna do ’bout it?

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:44.750
This shirt cost me ¥100,000.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:46.740
¥100,000?!

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:51.460
I’ll settle for ¥50,000 for the cleaning fees.

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:55.450
I don’t have that much on me right now.

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:57.970
How about ¥5,000?

00:14:57.970 --> 00:14:59.710
Are you mocking me?!

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:03.130
¥50,000! It won’t be pretty if you can’t pay!

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:05.310
¥3 should be plenty.

00:15:06.220 --> 00:15:08.300
Nah, maybe ¥500.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.080
What?

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:10.220
Irie-kun?

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:13.330
I’m talking about the cleaning fees for that cheap shirt.

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:14.730
What did you say?!

00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:18.320
This shirt is a Arel Laurel...
Err, what was it again?

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:22.480
A brand name you can’t even remember?

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.730
You must have bought it
on sale at a supermarket.

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:26.590
You little brat!

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:28.620
Sempai, it’s your turn.

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:32.860
I’m leaving the rest to you.

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:37.520
You were the one who exacerbated the problem.

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:41.360
Show Matsumoto what you’re made of.

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:43.720
Here.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.970
That’s mine!

00:15:47.970 --> 00:15:50.970
What are you blabbering about?!

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:53.980
Please get Sudou-sempai to take you home.

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:55.690
Irie-kun!

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:58.690
You dare do this to me?!

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:06.190
Bring it on, you hoodlum!

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:08.660
All of you are asking for it!

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:17.030
I just bought that racquet!

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:19.140
This is the finishing blow!

00:16:23.850 --> 00:16:26.040
Irie-kun, you noticed us?

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:29.930
With the dumb way you two were tailing me, I realized quickly.

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:31.990
I’m sorry.

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:36.100
After seeing you two together, I just...

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:38.680
But, if...

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:44.320
...you like Matsumoto-san...

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:48.730
Shall we go somewhere?

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:52.470
Yes!

00:16:57.180 --> 00:17:00.790
I can’t believe it.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:06.330
Irie-kun and I are...

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:11.770
I might have just used a lifetime’s worth of happiness today...

00:17:11.770 --> 00:17:13.920
I’m so happy right now.

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:17.940
There’s nothing but family here.

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:21.680
We’re the only couple on a boat.

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:23.200
Well, that’s because...

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:29.310
...there’s a well-known story that any couple who rides on the boats here will be jinxed and break up.

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:32.870
You didn’t know?

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:35.090
You’re kidding!

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:36.780
Idiot! Don’t stand up!

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:01.660
Wear this until it dries.

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:06.780
It was a clearance item, but better than staying wet, right?

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:08.470
Thanks.

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:14.830
I’m really sorry.

00:18:14.830 --> 00:18:19.220
I cause you nothing but trouble all the time.

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:22.150
Ever since I had my first memories...

00:18:22.150 --> 00:18:28.410
...I just can’t recall any difficult or bothersome moments.

00:18:29.050 --> 00:18:34.220
But, after I received your love letter during the senior year of high school...

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:38.300
...everyday was pretty much a struggle and an annoyance.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:44.460
When I think about it, perhaps you’re a trial presented to me.

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:45.560
Trial?

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:49.900
This is the first trial I’ve ever faced.

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:51.810
I thought of running away.

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:56.210
But recently, I’ve come to believe

00:18:56.210 --> 00:19:00.830
it’d be more interesting to face up to the trial than lead a life without any struggles.

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:03.530
I’m the trial, right?

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:05.590
You’re facing up to me?

00:19:05.590 --> 00:19:06.640
Yep.

00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:09.930
Life comes with both the good and the bad, I guess.

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:11.850
Face up to me?

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:15.880
He doesn’t mean pick a fight with me, right?

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:20.770
It’s okay if you don’t get it.

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:24.860
In other words, even though you tried to run away from me...

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:28.000
...but you changed your mind and now you...

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:31.470
Are you proposing?!

00:19:31.470 --> 00:19:34.260
How were you able to jump
to that conclusion?!

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:36.180
Eh? But...

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:39.980
I’m just saying that maybe it’s not so bad to be living in the same house.

00:19:39.980 --> 00:19:43.750
You don’t dislike me?

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:46.460
I may be quite awkward with you...

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:48.790
...but I don’t dislike you.

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:52.590
I love you, Irie-kun!

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:57.450
Ever since I was a high school freshman, you’ve been the only one I ever loved!

00:19:57.450 --> 00:19:58.590
I really love you!

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:02.980
I’m stupid, can’t cook...

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:05.860
...and also unglamorous, but I’ll work hard.

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:09.930
I’ll work hard with my cooking, my studies, and... and...

00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:11.110
I can’t wait.

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:15.780
You’re gonna try to become a talented woman for my sake?

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:20.460
For the time being, let’s see how you do for the first term exams.

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:26.440
Let’s make it so your test score would be proportional to the strength of your love.

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:32.090
I could manage an average
of about sixty points...

00:20:32.890 --> 00:20:36.910
Like always, the way he speaks
is a little mean...

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:40.930
...but his smile has changed a little from the time before.

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:44.270
Compared to the time I first gave Irie-kun the love letter...

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:46.790
Compared to the first time we kissed...

00:20:46.790 --> 00:20:50.220
I feel closer to Irie-kun now.

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:55.020
Dad?

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:00.690
Dad, what did you want to talk about?

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:05.670
Well, you see, Kotoko. It’s already been a year since we’ve been under the care of the Iries.

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:08.710
I’ve been thinking...

00:21:08.710 --> 00:21:15.280
...we can’t take advantage of Iri-chan and his wife’s kindness forever.

00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:17.220
So, what do you think?

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:25.050
Don’t you think it’s time to go back to living alone with your Dad?

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:28.020
Dad?

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:08.960
I heard, Kotoko!

00:23:08.960 --> 00:23:10.990
You’re finally leaving that idiot, Irie.

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:13.030
Keep quiet, you!

00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:15.170
Kotoko, I know you can’t help but feel sad.

00:23:15.170 --> 00:23:18.510
But, we can’t be under Iri-chan’s care forever.

00:23:18.510 --> 00:23:20.510
Yeah, that’s true...

00:23:20.510 --> 00:23:23.760
Dad, I understand, but...

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:25.970
Yuuki-kun, what’s wrong?

00:23:26.430 --> 00:23:28.580
Next time on Itazura na Kiss:

00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:30.450
Goodbye Rainy Day.

00:23:30.450 --> 00:23:32.460
I’m definitely gonna be happy.
